# Stable name for the front sign-detection camera.
#
# /dev/videoN is not stable for this device. On this hardware the Brio has been
# observed at video0, video1 and video2 across replugs, because the number depends
# on enumeration order and the camera claims two nodes (capture + metadata).
# camera_params.yaml previously hardcoded /dev/video0 and broke whenever the camera
# was moved to a different port.
#
# Matching on vendor:product rather than a by-id path keeps this valid across units:
# the by-id symlink embeds the camera's serial number, so it would only ever resolve
# on the one Jetson it was captured from.
#
# ATTR{index}=="0" picks the capture node; index 1 is the metadata node
# (V4L2_CAP_META_CAPTURE), which cannot stream video.
#
# TAG+="systemd" does two jobs. It makes systemd create a .device unit for this camera
# AND alias that unit to every entry in DEVLINKS -- which is what gives
# dev-camera\x2dfront.device its name, the name camera-sign-detect.service binds to. The
# BindsTo= there is what stops the pipeline on unplug, so dropping this tag would leave
# the detector running against a device that no longer exists.
#
# SYSTEMD_WANTS is the start edge, and it covers boot as well as a later replug:
# systemd-udev-trigger.service replays add events for devices that are already present.
# The unit itself has no [Install] section, so this rule is the only thing that ever
# starts it.
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTRS{idVendor}=="046d", ATTRS{idProduct}=="094c", ATTR{index}=="0", \
    SYMLINK+="camera-front", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}="camera-sign-detect.service"
